  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\nUpper trough will linger across central Canada through the next\nweek with an upper ridge over the Rockies. Various shortwaves will\nbe moving through the ridge over the next week, gradually\nflattening out the ridge. Over time this will bring cooler\ntemperatures and scattered showers. \n\nIn the short term, high pressure will bring light winds today.\nSaturday will see a slight jump in temperatures along with winds\nas a low pressure system moves across southern Montana. This also\nleads into critical fire conditions for the southwest Fire zones,\nand a Fire Weather Watch is in effect for Saturday afternoon and\nevening.\n\nAs the upper ridge flattens, and flow turns zonal, smoke will\nlikely return to northeast Montana for next week. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nNo changes to the NBM except to add smoke and haze for day 2.\n\nConfidence for upgrading the Fire Weather Watch is moderate,\nmainly dependent on the winds.",
